# What is deliberately not in this repository, and why. The README says the
# same in prose; this is the enforceable version.

# ---- other people's data, one download away -------------------------------
# The EEA's to distribute. scripts/01_check_environment.py prints the URL, and
# every stage that needs it says so rather than failing obscurely.
Data/
*.zip

# The legal texts are free from EUR-Lex and the Resmi Gazete, the papers from
# their publishers. We cite them; we do not redistribute them.
refs/

# ---- generated, and large --------------------------------------------------
# Rebuilt by scripts/00_run_all.py. derived/processed/ IS tracked: it is what
# scripts/99_audit.py recomputes every manuscript claim from, so a reader who
# does not download the release can still check the arithmetic.
derived/abox/
derived/interim/

# The manuscript as a single file and the figure bundle, both produced by the
# pipeline from the sources that are tracked.
paper/censo-manuscript.docx
paper/figures.zip

# ---- environment -----------------------------------------------------------
.venv*/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store

# A working snapshot, not history.
.baseline/

# publish/site is its own git repository -- the GitHub Pages deployment target
# that w3id.org redirects to. scripts/97_assemble_publish.py writes into it and
# scripts/99_audit.py checks it is current, but its history belongs to that
# repository and not to this one.
publish/site/
